<title>BELGIUM: PICANOL H1 PROFIT UP 58 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>PICANOL H1 PROFIT UP 58 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 150.1	   vs    94.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax cash-flow		412.4	   vs   241.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   250.1	   vs   124.7</p>
<p>    Turnover			 6,272.7	   vs 5,432.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian textile machinery maker Picanol NV said it</p>
<p>expected second-half results to evolve in line with those in the</p>
<p>first half provided currencies remained stable.</p>
<p>The first half profit rise was the result of improved</p>
<p>margins and efficiency, and the elimination of activities which</p>
<p>did not add value. The planned and steady improvement of</p>
<p>profitability should create the scope for further investment, it</p>
<p>said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
